CM_ "moto-platform platform CAN bus (classic CAN 500 kbps, 11-bit IDs, D-009). ID plan and E2E scheme: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 4 and docs/e2e-profile.md. Only our own nodes are on this bus.";
CM_ BU_ RT_CORE "STM32H755 Cortex-M7 domain controller (D-072); sole vehicle-bus tester, republishes vehicle signals (D-021). Owns both FDCANs: it passes 0x020, 0x022, 0x081 and 0x120 to the SAFETY partition through the E2E mailbox and forwards the partition's 0x023 and 0x082 to this bus verbatim, never re-signing them (D-072 item 4c).";
CM_ BU_ SAFETY "STM32H755 Cortex-M4 safety partition (D-072): cornering decision with its own IMU, blind spot, immobilizer, LED ring and mirror LEDs. It has no CAN controller; its frames cross the inter-core mailbox and rt-core relays them. A frozen counter or a timeout on 0x023/0x082 means the partition (or the relay) stopped.";
CM_ BU_ CONN "Bike ESP32-S3 connectivity + audio node; bridge to the phone and the helmet unit, which is BLE only and not on this bus (D-073).";
CM_ BU_ LINUX "Raspberry Pi 5 HPC (Kuksa, kuksa-can-provider).";
CM_ BU_ HIL_SIM "STM32F4 HIL restbus simulator; may impersonate any node on the bench.";
CM_ BU_ TESTER "Development/diagnostic tester (host PC).";
CM_ BO_ 32 "rt-core EKF lean (roll) angle estimate for the cornering decision (hardware-architecture 5b.2 Layer 2); reaches the safety partition through the mailbox (D-072 item 4c). Until the EKF has converged after a restart, rt-core sends LEAN_ANGLE_STATE=INVALID and QUALITY=0.";
CM_ SG_ 32 LEAN_ANGLE_STATE "Estimate state: ESTIMATED, CLAMPED to the physical range, or INVALID. There is no safe default lean angle: rt-core sends INVALID instead (D-029); 2 is reserved and must be treated as INVALID.";
CM_ SG_ 32 LEAN_ANGLE "Roll angle; positive = leaning right.";
CM_ SG_ 32 LEAN_ANGLE_QUALITY "Estimator confidence; 0 = no confidence.";
CM_ BO_ 33 "Vehicle speed republished by rt-core from CL250 DID 0xF40D (D-021). Not a safety-node input (D-041): the Layer 1 cornering decision needs no speed. It keeps its safety-range ID and E2E protection for its other consumers; no safety decision may be based on it.";
CM_ SG_ 33 VEHICLE_SPEED_VALID "1 = VEHICLE_SPEED holds an ECU sample younger than stale_after_ms of DID 0xF40D (uds/vehicle_cl250.yaml); 0 = no valid source value. E2E OK only proves the rt-core link is fresh; consumers that care about freshness also bound VEHICLE_SPEED_AGE.";
CM_ SG_ 33 VEHICLE_SPEED "Range 0-255 km/h = the range of DID 0xF40D (one byte, formula A). The source resolution is 1 km/h; the 0.01 scale does not add precision today and leaves room for a finer fused speed later (Q-015).";
CM_ SG_ 33 VEHICLE_SPEED_AGE "Age of the source sample when rt-core wrote this frame, counted from the send time of the oldest unanswered read of DID 0xF40D (D-051), so never younger than the ECU sample; nearest 10 ms, saturates at 2550 ms; an INVALID speed sends 2550 (D-056). It does not include the wait in the TX buffer (at most one write of rt-core): the worst case for a VALID frame at its consumer is stale_after_ms of DID 0xF40D + one cycle + one rt-core comms pass (about 351 ms).";
CM_ BO_ 34 "rt-core EKF road friction and total mass estimates for the cornering decision (hardware-architecture 5b.2 Layer 2); reaches the safety partition through the mailbox (D-072 item 4c). Until the EKF has converged after a restart, rt-core sends *_STATE=INVALID and QUALITY=0.";
CM_ SG_ 34 FRICTION_COEFF_STATE "Estimate state: ESTIMATED, CLAMPED to the physical range, DEFAULT fallback value, or INVALID. Consumers must never treat DEFAULT as ESTIMATED; the DEFAULT values are in limits/platform_limits.yaml (D-029).";
CM_ SG_ 34 TOTAL_MASS_STATE "Estimate state: ESTIMATED, CLAMPED to the physical range, DEFAULT fallback value, or INVALID. Consumers must never treat DEFAULT as ESTIMATED; the DEFAULT values are in limits/platform_limits.yaml (D-029).";
CM_ SG_ 34 FRICTION_COEFF "Estimated tyre-road friction coefficient mu (dimensionless).";
CM_ SG_ 34 TOTAL_MASS "Estimated total mass (vehicle + rider + load).";
CM_ BO_ 35 "Safety partition output status (D-072 item 4c): the cornering warning level and its source (D-041, D-042), both blind-spot sides (hardware-architecture 5b.1) and the immobilizer state. The M4 writes it into the mailbox; rt-core forwards it verbatim and stops when the slot is not updated. Informational for every receiver (logging, phone, helmet HUD, D-073): the safety outputs are the LED ring and mirror LEDs, driven by the partition itself. No receiver may show a safe state from it; a timeout or E2E error means no status is available, never GREEN or CLEAR. Raw 0 is the no-information value of every field (codegen rule), so a zero-initialised or never-written field reads as unavailable.";
CM_ SG_ 35 CORNERING_LEVEL "Level shown on the LED ring (D-041 item 1). UNAVAILABLE = no usable lean source (D-042 item 4). It comes with CORNERING_SOURCE = NONE and NONE comes with UNAVAILABLE; a receiver reads any other pairing (e.g. GREEN with NONE, UNAVAILABLE with EKF) as UNAVAILABLE. Test UNAVAILABLE by value, never by ordering.";
CM_ SG_ 35 CORNERING_SOURCE "Lean source of the decision: NONE = no usable source; EKF = rt-core 0x020/0x022 usable; OWN_IMU = the D-042 fallback, shown on the ring as DEGRADED. 3 is reserved and is read as NONE.";
CM_ SG_ 35 BSM_LEFT "Left blind-spot state (hardware-architecture 5b.1): UNAVAILABLE = radar or decision not usable (also before the blind spot is implemented); CLEAR = no vehicle (mirror green); PRESENT = a vehicle on that side (solid red); APPROACHING = a vehicle approaching while signalling or changing lanes towards that side (blinking red).";
CM_ SG_ 35 BSM_RIGHT "Right blind-spot state; same values as BSM_LEFT.";
CM_ SG_ 35 IMMOBILIZER_STATE "Starter-relay immobilizer (invariant 6). UNKNOWN = the partition does not know the relay position (at boot, without position feedback; a boot never pulses the relay). UNLOCKED = relay released, the starter-relay coil circuit passes and the engine can start (default). LOCKED = the starter-relay coil circuit is interrupted. AUTH_PENDING = a lock request or an authorization (NFC, PIN) is being decided; it ends within 10 s in LOCKED or UNLOCKED, and in UNLOCKED if no decision is reached. FAULT = immobilizer out of service. Values 5-7 are read as UNKNOWN.";
CM_ BO_ 129 "rt-core heartbeat (0x080 + node_id). The safety partition receives it through the mailbox (D-042 item 3, D-072 item 4c).";
CM_ BO_ 130 "Safety partition heartbeat (0x080 + node_id), written by the M4 into the mailbox and forwarded verbatim by rt-core (D-072 item 4c).";
CM_ BO_ 132 "connectivity-node heartbeat (0x080 + node_id).";
CM_ BO_ 133 "linux-node heartbeat (0x080 + node_id).";
CM_ SG_ 129 ERROR_COUNT "Faults detected since boot; saturates at 255.";
CM_ SG_ 129 UPTIME "Seconds since boot; saturates at 65535. A decrease means the node restarted.";
CM_ SG_ 130 ERROR_COUNT "Faults detected since boot; saturates at 255.";
CM_ SG_ 130 UPTIME "Seconds since boot; saturates at 65535. A decrease means the node restarted.";
CM_ SG_ 132 ERROR_COUNT "Faults detected since boot; saturates at 255.";
CM_ SG_ 132 UPTIME "Seconds since boot; saturates at 65535. A decrease means the node restarted.";
CM_ SG_ 133 ERROR_COUNT "Faults detected since boot; saturates at 255.";
CM_ SG_ 133 UPTIME "Seconds since boot; saturates at 65535. A decrease means the node restarted.";
CM_ BO_ 272 "CL250 engine values republished by rt-core from UDS DIDs 0xF40C/0xF442/0xF405/0xF411 (D-021, uds/vehicle_cl250.yaml). Scaling equals the J1979 source scaling.";
CM_ SG_ 272 ENGINE_SPEED "From DID 0xF40C, (A*256+B)/4.";
CM_ SG_ 272 BATTERY_VOLTAGE "From DID 0xF442, (A*256+B)/1000.";
CM_ SG_ 272 COOLANT_TEMP "From DID 0xF405, A-40.";
CM_ SG_ 272 THROTTLE_POS "From DID 0xF411, A*100/255 (raw byte carried unchanged).";
CM_ SG_ 272 ECU_PRESENT "1 = the ECU answered any UDS request within the ECU-absent timeout.";
CM_ BO_ 288 "QM requests from rt-core to the safety partition (D-072 item 4c), passed through the mailbox. E2E protects integrity only. Used by the immobilizer alone: it never gates or degrades the cornering decision, the blind spot, the LED ring or mirror LEDs, the D-042 source selection or the M4 power and clock state, and its E2E status is not a D-042 fallback criterion (codegen SAFETY_RX_QM_IMMOBILIZER). A missing, stale or invalid frame is no request and never changes the immobilizer state (D-072 item 7, user 2026-10-18). A release rt-core image fills it only from its own state, never from a frame received on the platform bus.";
CM_ SG_ 288 IGNITION_STATE "Ignition (key) state seen by rt-core power management; UNKNOWN until measured. 3 is reserved and is read as UNKNOWN. Only OFF lets the partition accept a lock; it can never cause a lock or an unlock by itself.";
CM_ SG_ 288 PARK_MODE "rt-core park mode (wake-on-motion watch, D-072 item 2); UNKNOWN until known. 3 is reserved and is read as UNKNOWN. Informational for the immobilizer; never a mode input to the safety functions.";
CM_ SG_ 288 IMMOBILIZER_LOCK_REQUEST "LOCK = the phone or park mode asks the partition to lock the starter relay; it is only a request. LOCK is 2 so that a single stuck bit cannot form it; 1 and 3 are reserved and are read as NONE. The partition counts a lock only on a NONE -> LOCK transition with E2E OK, after it has seen NONE with E2E OK since its own boot, with IGNITION_STATE = OFF and its own IMU stationary (D-072 item 7). There is no unlock request: unlocking is the partition's own decision (NFC, PIN, hidden bypass).";
